  "reason": "The key finding from completed experiments is that RNA-only multiprofile (config_041, acc=0.650) surprisingly outperforms multimodal multiprofile with the same RNA encoder, image encoder, and aggregation (config_011, acc=0.632). This suggests the image modality is not contributing positively under concat fusion. Config_043 is identical to config_011 except it replaces concat with weighted fusion, making it a clean single-variable test of whether the fusion strategy is the bottleneck. If weighted fusion closes or reverses the gap, it tells us the image modality has signal that concat fails to leverage; if it does not, it strengthens the case that resnet50 image features are not informative for this task. This is the highest-information next step because it directly isolates the fusion mechanism—the one untested design axis in the best-performing multimodal setup—without confounding changes to encoder, profile, or aggregation."
}

